1 . SUM OF FIRST NATURAL NUMBER => N = 5 => 1+2+3+4+5 = 15

import java.util.*;
public class Main{
    
    public static int Nnumber(int i , int sum , int N){
        
        if(i>N){
            return sum;
        }
        
        return Nnumber(i+1 , sum+i , N);
        
    }
    
    public static void main(String[] args){
        
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int N = sc.nextInt();
        
      int ans =  Nnumber(1,0,N);
      System.out.print(ans);
      
        
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void Nnumber(int i, int sum, int N) {
        if (i > N) {
            System.out.println(sum);
            return; // exit this call
        }
        Nnumber(i + 1, sum + i, N); // recursive call
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int N = 5;
        Nnumber(1, 0, N);
    }
}
Nnumber(1,0,5) is called → not base → calls Nnumber(2,1,5)

Nnumber(2,1,5) is called → not base → calls Nnumber(3,3,5)

Nnumber(3,3,5) is called → not base → calls Nnumber(4,6,5)

Nnumber(4,6,5) is called → not base → calls Nnumber(5,10,5)

Nnumber(5,10,5) is called → not base → calls Nnumber(6,15,5)

Nnumber(6,15,5) is called → base met → prints 15 → returns

Stack behavior here

Yes ✅ all those calls (1→2→3→4→5) are still sitting in the call stack when the base case runs.

BUT: after the base case prints and returns, each previous call also just returns without doing anything extra.

So the unwinding looks like this:
Call stack (deepest first):

Nnumber(6,15,5) -> base case -> prints 15 -> return
Nnumber(5,10,5) -> nothing after recursive call -> return
Nnumber(4,6,5)  -> return
Nnumber(3,3,5)  -> return
Nnumber(2,1,5)  -> return
Nnumber(1,0,5)  -> return
main ends

Key Difference from return version

In the return version, every function call was depending on the return value from the deeper call, so values had to bubble back.

In this void print version, nothing is bubbling back. Once the base case prints, the earlier calls just finish one by one without carrying values.


